<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lahaina</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lahaina is a town on the west coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maui">Maui</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hawaii">Hawaii</a>. Long a royal centre of Maui's chiefs, it served as the capital of the Kingdom of Hawaii from about 1820 to 1845, and in the mid-19th century it was a major port of the Pacific whaling fleet and a centre of missionary activity. Much of the historic town was destroyed by a wildfire in August 2023.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lahaina.jpg" alt="Lahaina" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Calbear22 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:L%C4%81hain%C4%81_oceanfront.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
